# braille

glyph braille-off 3 3
......
..@@..
......

glyph braille-on 3 3
/0@@0\
@@@@@@
\0@@0/

name-parts $braille-6dot = (|1)(|2**2)(|3**4)(|4**8)(|5**16)(|6**32)
name-parts $braille-8dot = (|1)(|2**2)(|3**4)(|4**8)(|5**16)(|6**32)(|7**64)(|8**128)

glyph braille-($braille-6dot) 8 16
ref braille-(off|on) 1 2
ref braille-(off|on**2) 1 6
ref braille-(off|on**4) 1 10
ref braille-(off|on**8) 5 2
ref braille-(off|on**16) 5 6
ref braille-(off|on**32) 5 10

glyph braille-x($braille-8dot) 8 16
ref braille-(off|on) 1 2
ref braille-(off|on**2) 1 6
ref braille-(off|on**4) 1 10
ref braille-(off|on**8) 5 2
ref braille-(off|on**16) 5 6
ref braille-(off|on**32) 5 10
ref braille-(off|on**64) 1 14
ref braille-(off|on**128) 5 14

map U+2800..283F = braille-($braille-6dot)
map U+2840..28FF = braille-x($braille-6dot)(7||7**64)(*64|8*128)

// use 8-dot layout only when there is at least one 8-dot character
remap braille-8dot : braille-x($braille-8dot) : braille-($braille-6dot) -> braille-x($braille-6dot)
remap braille-8dot-rev : braille-($braille-6dot) -> braille-x($braille-6dot) : braille-x($braille-8dot)

remap group braille-8dot
remap group braille-8dot-rev reversed after braille-8dot

feature calt for DFLT : braille-8dot
feature calt for DFLT : braille-8dot-rev

sample `Braille` `Cat`
